==================================================
Aleks T. Mitkov  
Portfolio Project #1  
Direct-to-Consumer Eyewear Funnel Analysis (SQL + Python)
Product Funnel, A/B Testing, and Preference-Based Conversion
February 7, 2026  
==================================================

This project analyzes user behavior across Warby Parker’s onboarding and purchase funnels using SQL and Python. The focus is on understanding where users drop off, how product design choices affect conversion, and what insights can be drawn from preferences shown during onboarding.

All data used in this project is fictional and provided as part of a Code Academy case study developed in collaboration with Warby Parker’s Data Science team.


Project Structure
-----------------
This repository follows a production-style analytics workflow:

- queries.sql  
  Contains the core SQL logic used to explore funnel behavior directly in the database, including:
  - Survey question completion rates
  - End-to-end funnel conversion (Quiz → Home Try-On → Purchase)
  - A/B test logic for the Home Try-On experiment (3 pairs vs 5 pairs)

- analysis_funnel.py  
  Recreates the core funnel logic in Python, computes conversion metrics, and generates:
  - A conversion funnel visualization
  - A survey completion funnel visualization
  - A CSV file containing key conversion rates

- analysis_ab_test.py  
  Analyzes the Home Try-On A/B test by comparing purchase conversion rates for users who received:
  - 3 pairs
  - 5 pairs  
  Outputs a bar chart and a summary table suitable for reporting.

- analysis_style_preference.py  
  Examines how stated style preferences from the quiz (Men’s, Women’s, “Not sure”) relate to purchase behavior and visualizes conversion rates by preference.
- Raw_Data
    - home_try_on.csv
    - purchase.csv
    - quiz.csv
    - survey.csv
    - build_db_wp.py  
    Utility script used to construct the SQLite database locally from raw CSV files.

- warby_parker.db  
  SQLite database containing the four core tables from above (purchase, home_try_on, quiz, and survey)

- outputs/  
  Directory containing all generated figures and tables used for analysis and reporting.

- wp_deliverable.pdf  
  Presentation-style summary of the analysis, consolidating key metrics, visualizations, and other insights derived from the SQL and Python workflows in this repository.


Data Overview
-------------
The dataset represents multiple stages of the Warby Parker funnel:

- survey  
  Stores question-level quiz interactions, with one row per user response.
  This table is used to analyze quiz completion behavior and identify where users drop off between questions.

- quiz  
  Stores finalized quiz outcomes, with one row per user.
  Each column represents the user’s selected preference after completing the quiz.

- home_try_on  
  Records users who participated in the Home Try-On program, including the number of pairs sent.

- purchase  
  Records completed purchases and serves as the bottom of the funnel.


Key Analyses
------------
- Survey Completion Funnel  
  Identifies which quiz questions correspond to the largest user drop-off.

- Conversion Funnel  
  Measures:
    - Quiz → Home Try-On conversion
    - Home Try-On → Purchase conversion
    - Overall Quiz → Purchase conversion

- Home Try-On A/B Test  
  Evaluates whether sending more pairs increases purchase conversion.

- Style Preference Analysis  
  Explores whether self-reported style preferences correlate with purchase behavior.


Notes
-----
- All analysis is reproducible and executed locally using SQLite and Python.
- Static Plotly image export requires the kaleido package.
- This project is intended to demonstrate analytics and data engineering skills and does not reflect real Warby Parker business data or performance.
